Fallout of #79, and deliberately not blocking it.

maint/spec-to-type.pl's curation list ends with:

  the swagger gives this field no description at all (199)

Each of those attributes carries `Undocumented upstream.` in its =attr
block and nothing invented -- which is correct and honest, and also 199
places where a reader learns nothing.

Where the swagger gives an `example`, appending it mechanically was
considered and rejected: the example explains the field only sometimes,
and that judgement is not one a rule should make 199 times.

The work: go through them by hand, in order of how often a caller
actually touches the class, and write what the field is from a measured
engine response plus what this distribution already knows. Anything that
stays genuinely unknown keeps the honest line -- an invented sentence is
worse than an admission.

Get the list with:
  perl maint/spec-to-type.pl --verify /tmp/x   (curation list at the end)

Anything written here must go into maint/spec-to-type-prose.yaml, not
into the generated file, or --verify stops being empty.

Done in six commits, 0bba2aa / ea96f94 / 5410214 / 713e8e1 / 4822cde and the correction 47ee981. 192 of 199 fields described, 7 left standing with nothing invented -- ContainerState.error, EndpointPortConfig.name, Plugin::Config.ipc_host and pid_host, PluginDevice.name and description, PluginPrivilege.description. The 'Undocumented upstream.' marker stays and the description follows it, so a reader sees at a glance what came from Docker and what came from us. Two spec contradictions recorded rather than smoothed, and a third after I measured GET /images/{id}/history: the swagger's example shows a bare digest, the engine sends sha256:<missing> on nine of ten layers, which is a marker and not an id -- handing it to GET /images/{id}/json looks up nothing. The agent corrected one of its own generalisations in the same pass (a #(nop) COPY layer reports a non-zero size). It also caught me: I wrote API 1.41 from my curl path prefix, and the engine announces 1.44 -- .claude/rules/api-docker-rules.md carried the same error and is fixed.
